From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VyOS LS1046A CI <ci@vyos-ls1046a>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 23:12:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vpp: ARM64 resource defaults — cap main-heap-size and buffers

Upstream VyOS defaults main-heap-size=3G which requires ~3.2GB of
hugepages. The LS1046A has 7.4GB total RAM with 4GB in hugepages and
needs the kernel + OS to share the remaining ~3.4GB.

Override for ARM64/LS1046A:
  main-heap-size:  3G → 256M   (256M is the minimum, sufficient for AF_XDP)
  buffers-per-numa: auto → 16384 (prevents auto-calc allocating 32768+)

With these defaults VPP needs ~1GB in hugepages (256M heap + 128M stats
+ 32M buffers), not ~3.2GB.

---
diff --git a/interface-definitions/vpp.xml.in b/interface-definitions/vpp.xml.in
--- a/interface-definitions/vpp.xml.in
+++ b/interface-definitions/vpp.xml.in
@@ -229,7 +229,7 @@
                         <regex>(auto)</regex>
                       </constraint>
                     </properties>
-                    <defaultValue>auto</defaultValue>
+                    <defaultValue>16384</defaultValue>
                   </leafNode>
                   <leafNode name="data-size">
                     <properties>
@@ -303,7 +303,7 @@
                       <help>Main heap size</help>
                       #include <include/unformat_memory_size.xml.i>
                     </properties>
-                    <defaultValue>3G</defaultValue>
+                    <defaultValue>256M</defaultValue>
                   </leafNode>
                   <leafNode name="main-heap-page-size">
                     <properties>
